import { CollectionTransformCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> CollectionTransformCopy = CollectionTransformCopy {
  summary: "items.concat joins the Arrays inside an Array, removing one level of nesting. It preserves outer and inner order, and an empty Array contributes no elements.",
  taskTitle: "Combine separate task batches into one list",
  purpose: "Join the batch containing Read, an empty batch, and the batch containing Review and Ship. Turn those three groups into one Array ordered Read, Review, Ship.",
  typescriptBefore: "batches.flat() flattens one level of nested arrays. The empty middle array contributes no elements, and the other elements keep their order. This task already takes a short, idiomatic line in TypeScript.",
  benefit: "Seseragi concat also combines several Arrays that are already grouped together. The input is Array<Array<String>> and the result is Array<String>, making the single removed level visible in the types.",
  setup: "items is the alias for std/array, and let batches names the grouped tasks. Each element of the outer [ ... ] is itself an Array. The middle [] is an empty Array between the other two batches.",
  after: [
    "items.concat batches calls the function by placing its argument after the name, separated by a space. It takes elements from [\"Read\"], then [], then [\"Review\", \"Ship\"], producing [\"Read\",\"Review\",\"Ship\"].",
    "The comprehension [value | value <- ...] takes each element of the concat result as value and creates a display Array. The values and their order stay the same when that Array is displayed as JSON.",
    "concat changes neither batches nor the Arrays it contains. Receive the combined list as its return value and use it for display or further processing.",
  ],
  details: [
    "Only one nesting level is removed. For example, [[[1], [2]], [], [[3]]] becomes [[1], [2], [3]]. The inner [1], [2], and [3] are still Arrays rather than being flattened all the way to integers.",
    "An empty outer Array gives an empty result. A collection containing only empty Arrays also gives an empty result. A value appearing in several batches is kept each time.",
    "concat requires an Array whose elements are Arrays. An Array of integers such as [1, 2, 3] cannot be passed. If the types do not match, check whether the input is already a single list of elements.",
    "Use append to join just two Arrays, or flatMap to extract an Array from each record before joining. concat itself takes no function to choose what to extract.",
  ],
}
